  "source": "What lunaRun itself installs: the Windows list of extensions its generated php.ini switches on (crates/luna-core/src/runtimes/php_config.rs, WINDOWS_EXTENSIONS, a test keeps the two in step) plus opcache, the extensions compiled into the official Windows build, and the extension set of the static-php-cli `common` build used on macOS and Linux (docs/RUNTIMES.md, checked 2026-11-02).",
  "note": "Keys are the Composer names (`ext-pdo_mysql` is `pdo_mysql`, `ext-zend-opcache` is `zend-opcache`, always lower case). `windows` and `unix` say what the PHP that lunaRun installs has: `enabled` (loaded), `disabled` (shipped as a loadable extension that lunaRun does not switch on), `absent` (not in the build; a static build cannot load extensions). A name that is not in this table is reported as `unknown`: it is not a statement that it is missing. `ini` is the name in php.ini when it differs from the key, `zend` marks `zend_extension=`.",
